Subject: [PATCH] fix(provider): clone copies the Resolve map so a diff of two
 snapshots sees its edits (#6734)

clone() copied every other map and slice but left Resolve shared with the
original. Edit-style callers build was and now from clone() and store the
diff: a Resolve change lands in both snapshots, storedChanges sees none,
and the second "provider set resolve.<host>=..." is dropped without an
error.

Upstream's own Save path writes the whole provider and never diffs, which
is why the landed provider set resolve tests never caught it; qiqll's
provider Edit (#5914 tree) was the first caller to trip - its
TestProviderSetResolve is stably red there and green once clone() copies
Resolve.

Run: go test -run TestProviderCloneCopiesResolve ./internal/provider - red
before, green after; ablation (block removed) red at provider_clone_test.go:19
("clone shares the inner slice..."); full ./internal/provider ok but the
standing TestResolveVia (host proxy, same red on the base commit); -race on
the new test ok; gofmt/vet clean; GOOS linux/windows/darwin nogui builds ok.

